CAT = "phnapValues"; SEG = "VAL"
Q = [
("The PNP's core values are Maka-Diyos, Makabayan, Makatao and:",
 "Makakalikasan", ["Makapangyarihan", "Makabago", "Makatarungan"],
 "The four PNP core values, also adopted by the PNP Academy, are Maka-Diyos, Makabayan, Makatao and Makakalikasan (God-centered, patriotic, humane, caring for the environment)."),
("A motorist stopped for beating a red light offers you money to let him go. What should you do?",
 "Refuse and issue the ticket", ["Accept and let him go", "Ask for a larger amount", "Let him go with a stern warning"],
 "Accepting money to drop an enforcement action is bribery. Letting him go for no reason also fails the duty to enforce the law fairly."),
("While on checkpoint duty you find a wallet with cash and an ID on the road. What should you do?",
 "Record it and turn it over", ["Keep the cash as a reward", "Leave it where you found it", "Give it to the first claimant"],
 "Logging the find and turning it over lets the owner, named on the ID, recover it. Handing it to the first person who asks risks giving it to the wrong person."),
("A superior tells you to change the time in your incident report to cover up a late response. What should you do?",
 "Refuse and report it properly", ["Change it as ordered", "Ask a colleague to make the change", "Destroy the original report"],
 "Falsifying an official report is dishonest and unlawful even when ordered. A lawful order never requires a false record."),
("A woman comes to the station saying her husband beat her and she is afraid to go home. What should be done first?",
 "Protect her and refer her case", ["Tell her to settle it at home", "Ask her to come back tomorrow", "Call her husband to the station"],
 "Her safety comes first, and the women and children protection desk handles abuse cases. Sending her home or calling the husband in may put her at risk."),
("You notice a fellow officer drinking alcohol while on duty. What is the best action?",
 "Report it to the supervisor", ["Join him to avoid conflict", "Ignore it just this one time", "Post about it online"],
 "Drinking on duty endangers the public and the officer. Reporting through the chain of command deals with it properly; posting online does not."),
("A colleague wants to post photos of a crime victim's body on social media. What is the proper response?",
 "Advise against posting them", ["Share them to warn the public", "Post them with the name hidden", "Send them to the victim's family"],
 "Crime scene photos are evidence and posting them violates the victim's dignity and privacy. They belong in the case file only."),
("While patrolling, an elderly resident asks you for directions to the health center. How should you respond?",
 "Give clear directions politely", ["Tell him you are too busy", "Point vaguely and walk on", "Refer him to the barangay hall"],
 "Courtesy and help in small things build the public's trust in the police, and it costs only a moment."),
("You are assigned to investigate a theft in which your cousin is the suspect. What should you do?",
 "Tell your superior and step aside", ["Handle the case quietly", "Warn your cousin first", "Close the case for lack of evidence"],
 "A relative as suspect is a conflict of interest. Disclosing it and stepping aside keeps the investigation fair and trusted."),
("A store owner offers officers free meals every day 'for keeping the area safe'. What is the proper response?",
 "Politely decline the offer", ["Accept it as a token of thanks", "Accept it on weekends only", "Ask for cash instead"],
 "Regular gifts for doing one's duty create a sense of owing a favor, which compromises fair service. Officers are already paid to keep the area safe."),
("Under the Public Assembly Act, police officers at a lawful rally must exercise:",
 "maximum tolerance", ["immediate dispersal", "full force", "selective arrests"],
 "Batas Pambansa Blg. 880 requires authorities to observe maximum tolerance, the highest degree of restraint, toward peaceful assemblies."),
("Neighbors help a family move their house to higher ground before the rainy season. Which Filipino value does this show?",
 "Bayanihan", ["Pakikisama", "Utang na loob", "Amor propio"],
 "Bayanihan is the spirit of community cooperation, named after neighbors carrying a house together. Utang na loob is a debt of gratitude."),
]
